<title>SPAIN: Spain Ibex-35 index welcomes three newcomers.</title>
<headline>Spain Ibex-35 index welcomes three newcomers.</headline>
<dateline>MADRID 1997-06-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Spanish steel tube producer Tubacex, zinc producer Asturiana del Zinc and sausage skin maker Viscofan will join the Ibex-35 index of leading shares from July 1, an Ibex committee spokesman said on Monday.</p>
<p>At the same time, Spanish property company Metrovacesa, electricity firm Gesa and construction firm Grupo Acciona will leave the index to make way for the newcomers, the committee said.</p>
<p>The constituent companies of the Ibex index are reassessed twice yearly in January and July by a committee made up of five representatives from the Stock Exchange authority, the MEFF futures exchange and market experts. The committee does not make public the criteria it uses.</p>
<p>Tubacex ended 48 pesetas up at 440 on Monday, while Asturiana was 50 pesetas higher at 2,840 and Viscofan 10 pesetas down at 3,250. The Ibex-35 index closed 40.03 points higher, 0.59 percent, to 6,801.95.</p>
